# Chunk Selection Strategy

Never retrieve a fixed number.

Instead allocate a token budget.

Example

```
Available

40,000 tokens

Workspace

2,000

Feature

5,000

Story

2,000

Repository

8,000

Retrieved Documents

15,000

Instructions

2,000

Expected Response

6,000
```

This prevents prompt overflow.

---

# Parent Chunk Expansion

Suppose vector search returns

```
Page 18

Rule 4
```

Often the surrounding sections are needed.

Automatically include

```
Page 17

Page 18

Page 19
```

or

```
Section

Settlement Validation
```

instead of just one isolated paragraph.

This gives Claude the surrounding context.

---

# Chunk Relationships

Store links between chunks.

```
BRD

↓

Business Rules

↓

Validation Rules

↓

Error Codes

↓

Acceptance Criteria
```

If one chunk is selected, you can optionally include its parent or siblings when there is available token budget.

---

# Repository + Document Fusion

Don't search documents and repositories separately.

Merge them.

Example

Story

↓

Relevant API

↓

Controller

↓

Business Rule

↓

Excel Mapping

↓

Database Table

↓

Previous Story

↓

Technical Design

↓

AI

````

Claude receives a unified context rather than disconnected sources.

---

# Citation Support

Keep references with every retrieved chunk.

Example

```json
{
  "document": "BRD.docx",
  "page": 27,
  "section": "Payment Validation",
  "chunkId": "c281",
  "score": 0.94
}
````

Claude can then generate responses like:

> Add validation for settlement cutoff (Source: BRD.docx, Page 27).

This is valuable for auditability.

